course: dictionary
lesson: 7778
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Pygmy» can name a very small kind of animal, it can be an old word for some peoples, and it can be an insult. The context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «There are hundreds of kinds of monkeys, from a pygmy marmoset that could sit on your finger to a mandrill heavier than a big dog.» The comparison is the clue. A pygmy marmoset is much smaller than its relatives, so pygmy here means a very small kind of animal.
explain: When pygmy comes before an animal name, such as «pygmy goat» or «pygmy shrew», it means a small kind of that animal. When it describes people, it is an old word that many people now find offensive. Use the names the peoples use themselves, such as the Mbuti or Baka.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a very small kind of goat» fit? Then you have it.
fact: Pygmy means very small when it names a kind of animal or plant, such as the pygmy hippopotamus.
fact: «Pygmy» was an old word for some short peoples of Central Africa, and many people now see it as offensive.
fact: Respectful way: use the names of the peoples themselves, such as the Mbuti or Baka.
fact: «Pygmy» is also an informal insult for a person thought to be unimportant.
fact: A pygmy marmoset from the Amazon weighs about 100 grams, so it is one of the smallest monkeys.
exercise: In «a pygmy marmoset that could sit on your finger», what does pygmy mean? | *A very small kind of monkey | A person thought to be unimportant | A monkey that lives high in the trees only at night | A large, strong monkey
exercise: In «the coral reef pygmy goby», what does pygmy mean? | A kind of coral | A fish that is very old | A person who lives by the sea | *A very small kind of goby fish
exercise: Ella says, «You're just a pygmy in this team.» What does pygmy mean here? | A tall, strong player | An old name for a rainforest | A very small kind of goat | *A person thought to be unimportant
test: «The pygmy goat stood by the fence, no taller than my knee.» What does pygmy mean? | A very old goat | A goat that gives lots of milk | *A very small kind of goat | A person who is unimportant
test: Jayden says pygmy always means tiny. Is he right? | Yes, but only for fish | *No, it has other meanings, so check the context | Yes, it always means tiny | No, it means very tall
exam: When talking about the people once called pygmies, which word is respectful? | the pygmies | the little ones | *the Mbuti | the short folk
